{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms","id":922985,"title":"[Ex3] Lunar Size, Strength, Limits, and Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T19:06:17-07:00","id":922985,"title":"[Ex3] Lunar Size, Strength, Limits, and Charms","content":"<b><u>SHAPESHIFTING </u>(page 545)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A Lunar may pay four motes to assume any form he has taken. This transformation lasts indefinitely, until the Lunar reverts to his true human form (which is free and reflexive) or shifts into a different shape. Shapeshifting can be flurried, but not with an attack.<br /> <br /> Animal forms grant the Lunar access to all physical dice pools, as well as the animal\u2019s special attacks and Merits. Latent or magical abilities are not granted by shapeshifting, but can be unlocked with training or Charms. Animals with Legendary Size are beyond the skill of most young Lunar shapeshifters, though this limitation can be overcome.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>LUNAR EXCELLENCIES</b></u><b> (545)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Lunar Exalted tap into the raw potential of their Attributes to bolster their heroic feats, and can add up to (Attribute) dice to any action. However, with a stunt, they may add a second Attribute to the limit as long as the action is described in a way that fits the combination. For example, a Full Moon rolling (Dexterity + Brawl) to smash a Dragon-Blooded shikari would normally have a dice limit of (Dexterity), but could increase this to (Dexterity + Strength) if he described the attack in a way that evoked his raw brawn and mighty thews.<br /> <br /> When raising static values, Lunars can add up to (Attribute)/2, rounded down to the static value. With a stunt, they can draw upon a second Excellency, allowing them to add up to (Attribute + Second Attribute)/2, round down. Thus, a Dexterity 5, Dodge 5, and Intelligence 5 Lunar who attempts to evade an attack and describes how his keen mind discerns the rhythm of his opponent\u2019s blows, helping him to avoid them, could raise his Evasion by up to 5.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The Corebook does not specify how these two rules intersect, but I have a proposal.<br /> <br /> When the Lunar wears a form with a dice-pool larger than his own, each extra die counts against his dice-adding limit. When the Lunar stunts to add a second Excellency to his action, it is limited by his own natural Attribute score, even if it would be greater or lesser than that of the creature whose form he wears.<br /> <br /> Thus, a Strength 5, Athletics 5, and Stamina 5 Lunar who is currently a yeddim can only add one more die to his action with just his Strength Excellency alone. But stunting to include his Stamina Excellency will allow him to add a total of six more dice.<br /> <br /> If that same character is the form of a clawstrider and wants to apply his Stamina Excellency to improve his soak against a Withering attack, he cannot increase the static value of 7 at all. But stunting to include his Strength Excellency will allow him to add a total of 3 more points.<br /> <br /> These limitations should apply even if the form is the Lunar's own spirit shape, so as to remove mechanical incentives towards certain Totems and also avoid disincentives regarding any other sorts of Totems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further, I wonder if the Charm which allows Lunars to assume the forms of creatures with Legendary Size should be more limited than the Towering Beast Form of past Editions; perhaps more like God-Beast Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Perhaps assuming the form of a creature with Legendary Size should not be allowed to flurry with any action, should cost at least one Willpower point, and perhaps should cost a certain number of motes per turn.<br /> <br /> In this way, a Lunar is still rewarded for having a gigantic, battle-worthy beast form, but encouraged to use humbler forms more often. A Lunar with a Tyrant Lizard Totem would usually prefer to use his Deadly Beastman shape for most of a fight, reserving his Spirit Shape for specific moments.<br /> <br /> For those Lunar fans inspired by characters such as Beast Boy, consider how little time he ever spends in the form of elephants, giant dinosaurs, and other megafauna. It should also be especially easy for fans of <i>Steven Universe</i> to imagine that &quot;a power that big, comes with a bigger expense&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, let's examine some ideas for Lunar Strength Charms!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Undeniable Might</b> - If your own Strength-based dice pool is larger than that provided by your stolen form, you may use that instead, but your Tell becomes more obvious. Even if another character has never seen your Tell before, they may make the disguise-checking roll to notice it.<br /> <br /> <b>Devastating Ogre Enhancement</b> - for the rest of the scene, the Lunar swells to twice her mass, her bones thickening and her muscles doubling. Her Strength and Stamina are increased, but the bonuses count against her Excellency dice-adding limits.<br /> <br /> <b>Emperor Ox Expansion</b> - for the duration of one attack or feat of strength, the Lunar explodes in size, striking with far greater mass, lifting with superior leverage, or absorbing damage with thicker flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Flash Might Methodology</b> - for a single feat of strength, the Lunar can add a number of successes equal to the lesser of his Essence or Strength ratings, and does not need a stunt to justify adding his Stamina Excellency to his Strength Excellency.<br /> <br /> <b>Mountainous Spirit Expression</b> - the Lunar may use Heart's Blood to reflexively shapeshift into a creature larger than a man, but not so large as to have the Legendary Size merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Hyena Jaw Technique</b> -- This Charm allows a Lunar who crashes an opponent in a grapple to reflexively shapeshift into a form big enough to swallow her victim whole... or at least enclose them entirely within her jaws. The Lunar must have the Heart's Blood of a creature big enough for the job.<br /> <br /> <b>Towering Beast Form</b> - the Lunar may use the stolen Heart's Blood of a creature with the Legendary Size merit. Shapeshifting into such a form requires an action which cannot be flurried, costs one Willpower and two more motes to start, and costs two more motes each turn until the Lunar assumes a form without Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> <b>God-Beast Transcendence</b> - the Lunar may now flurry another action -- including an attack -- with an action to shapeshift into a creature with the Legendary Size merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Body-Breaking Kata</b> - the Lunar enjoys bonuses to damage and grappling control rolls against an opponent who is only half her size or smaller<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-07-2016, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:47:25-07:00","id":923007,"title":"","content":"<b>BIRTH OF FLIGHT</b><br /> <i>3m, 1i; Supplemental, Instant; Decisive-only; Strength 3, Essence 1 \u2013 ???</i><br /> <br /> This supplements a decisive attack at any range. An enemy damaged by this Charm is knocked prone. This force is sufficient to end a rush against any target.<br /> <br /> If this Charm supplements a Decisive smashing attack, this Charm waives its Initiative cost, and doubles 10s on the Initiative damage roll.<br /> <br /> If this Charm supplements the special attack of a stolen form which can mimic the effects of the Heaven Thunder Hammer Solar Charm, this Charm waives its Initiative cost, and doubles 9s on the Initiative roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what happens when the Lunar learns an advanced Strength Charm which allows him to perform a trick like Heaven Thunder Hammer regardless of his form... and then he uses it <i>with</i> the HTH-like special attack of an animal form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:03:54-07:00","id":923020,"title":"","content":"I agree with your idea about excellencies, that seems sensible.<br /> <br /> The idea of spending motes every turn you're in a giant form... I think that could work in combat, but I kind of feel like Lunars ought to be able to use big forms for stuff outside of combat. But the wp I think could work well. You had to do that for human forms in 2nd ed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:54:14-07:00","id":923042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=923020#post923020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of spending motes every turn you're in a giant form... I think that could work in combat, but I kind of feel like Lunars ought to be able to use big forms for stuff outside of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot about that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T19:20:57-07:00","id":923635,"title":"","content":"Given that Lunar Exalted have ways of increasing their effective Strength score just by using an Excellency or assuming an animal form (and given that these can be used for attack damage in ways that Solar Athletics lifting Charms cannot), I think the Lunar version of Strength Increasing Exercise could offer only a FLAT increase, as opposed to the Solar's Charm's variable increase.<br /> <br /> The bonus Strength dot should also count against the Lunar's dice-adding limit, just like the higher dice-pools of a stronger animal form.<br /> <br /> <br /> I might also suggest the possibility that &quot;Devasting Ogre Enhancement&quot; be canceled if the Lunar shapeshifts into anything but his human or DBT Form; thus a Lunar chooses to fight as a really beefy tiger, or he conserves his motes and fights more flexibly as any number of beasts.<br /> <br /> This might be the pattern for various other Charms, like Armor-Forming Technique, Grasping Pseudopod Method (tentacles), Snake Head Defense (snake hair), and &quot;Grow Wings Prana&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:22:34-07:00","id":925526,"title":"","content":"So, regarding my concerns with Heaven Thunder Hammer... I forgot that it can only be used with Decisive attacks, and Decisive attacks roll Initiative regardless of Strength. A Lunar in a large and powerful form can gain and retain Initiative more easily, but cannot necessarily leverage it better than a human-form opponent. Especially if Solars have superior Charms for enhancing Decisive damage.<br /> <br /> There is still the issue that Lunars can produce the effects of the Charm through the non-magical tail attacks of dinosaurs. If the Lunar Exalted get anything like HTH, it needs to stack with those attacks without breaking the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm favoring the idea of &quot;Impressions of Strength&quot; being a Reflexive Charm that lets a Lunar apply their Strength Excellency to their Initiative rolls for Decisive attacks and appropriate Gambits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:15:38-07:00","id":925573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925526#post925526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Lunar Exalted get anything like HTH, it needs to stack with [dinosaur tail attacks]\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I'm not sure they need to stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:23:57-07:00","id":925611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925573#post925573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I'm not sure they need to stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is a Charmless action and the other is a reflexive Charm. There is no reason they cannot be used together, so one must consider what happens when they stack.<br /> <br /> One also needs to remember that, generally, Lunar attack Charms work with any sort of attack, so the Lunar HTH needs to be adjusted for use with shuriken and arrows.<br /> <br /> My concern isn't &quot;the tail attacks make Lunar HTH better&quot; but &quot;Lunar HTH is going to make those tail attacks better.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:29:03-07:00","id":925616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925611#post925611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One also needs to remember that, generally, Lunar attack Charms work with any sort of attack...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they need to? We're moving into a new edition, must this assumption go unquestioned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:44:19-07:00","id":925622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925616#post925616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they need to? We're moving into a new edition, must this assumption go unquestioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Were you around for First Edition, where they *did* split Lunar Charms into Unarmed, Melee, and Projectiles?<br /> <br /> I don't want to split the Strength attack Charms into four different branches for each attack Ability. I feel Lunar Charms should be more flexible in application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:46:53-07:00","id":925624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925622#post925622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were you around for First Edition, where they *did* split Lunar Charms into Unarmed, Melee, and Projectiles?<br /> <br /> I don't want to split the Strength attack Charms into four different branches for each attack Ability. I feel Lunar Charms should be more flexible in application.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that he's suggesting that it get split up into the same narrow categories as 1e. Just that it, say, gets toned down to where the Alchemicals are, where attack and defense are broader but not universally omni-applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T13:46:55-07:00","id":926059,"title":"","content":"One of the big problems I have with these 'proposals' is that the whole reason animals are as strong as they are is to make them look like potent, very useful things for a Lunar. The developers have explicitly stated the reason a bear is stronger than even the greatest mortal swordsman to ever live in a fight, is so it looks good for a Lunar to turn into one, and so that shapeshifting into straight up animal forms is always useful. The Tyrant Lizard is able to beat up first circle demons with ease because a Lunar turning into one is supposed to be the Scariest Fucker In Town.<br /> <br /> The proposals of all these limitations on how scary these animal shapes actually are seems to go against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:14:52-07:00","id":926078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=926059#post926059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big problems I have with these 'proposals' is that the whole reason animals are as strong as they are is to make them look like potent, very useful things for a Lunar. The developers have explicitly stated the reason a bear is stronger than even the greatest mortal swordsman to ever live in a fight, is so it looks good for a Lunar to turn into one, and so that shapeshifting into straight up animal forms is always useful. The Tyrant Lizard is able to beat up first circle demons with ease because a Lunar turning into one is supposed to be the Scariest Fucker In Town.<br /> <br /> The proposals of all these limitations on how scary these animal shapes actually are seems to go against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do any of these proposals make the animal forms less useful with Lunar magic than without it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:18:24-07:00","id":927825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925616#post925616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they need to? We're moving into a new edition, must this assumption go unquestioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=925624#post925624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that he's suggesting that it get split up into the same narrow categories as 1e. Just that it, say, gets toned down to where the Alchemicals are, where attack and defense are broader but not universally omni-applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, there could at least be different Charms for inflicting knockback with projectile and non-projectile attacks. If necessary.<br /> <br /> But can Count Alucard offer a reason why the Lunar version of Heaven Thunder Hammer, however humble it may be, should not be able to supplement the special tail attacks of the Pestetail or Siege Lizard?<br /> <br /> Or that, if these attacks can be supplemented by such a Charm, the Charm should not be able to improve upon their effects, however small that improvement might be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:59:55-07:00","id":927840,"title":"","content":"Because the attack already inflicts the effect in question. If an attack has an effect of &quot;knocks you on your ass,&quot; a Charm that adds an effect of &quot;knocks you on your ass&quot; isn't going to do anything - <i>you're already on your ass</i>. <br /> <br /> If a Solar somehow had access to a pestletail's tail attack, I probably wouldn't make it compatible with Heaven Thunder Hammer either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:25:32-07:00","id":927853,"title":"","content":"I disagree, but I have no acceptable rebuttal prepared. Instead, I will address another idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar Exalted can use the Charm &quot;Devil-Stranging Attitude&quot; to execute grappling attack rolls with their Strength instead of their Dexerity; &quot;Ascendant Battle Visage&quot; likewise allows a Solar to roll Rush actions with Strength instead of Dexterity.<br /> <br /> On the face of it, I thought that Lunar Exalted would not get as much out of such an effect, because many Lunars would be spending their time in animal forms, which have QC fixed dice-pools without clear Attribute scores. Without knowing precisely what a Tyrant Lizard's individual Dexterity, Strength and Brawl scores would be, one cannot do that.<br /> <br /> However, it make sense to bundle that effect together with the ability to substitute your own nature dice-pool for an action taken in an animal form, when your natural dice-pool is larger.* Your Strength + Athletics dice-pool for Rushing can be higher than a bear's combat movement dice-pool of 6.<br /> <br /> The effect could further be bundled with an effect that allows you to add your Strength Excellency to a Dexterity-based Rush action without needing to think of a stunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I'd like this to be mirrored with social and mental Attribute Charms that let you use the social and mental Attributes of the people whose faces you wear, when those are greater than your own. But, this should bear a price beyond just motes and Willpower.<br /> <br /> Thinking of this price is why I suggested that using physical dice-pools beyond what a form should be capable carries a price; in their case, revealing your Tell enough that people can make a roll to see it even if they've never seen it before. Which they otherwise wouldn't be able to do, since you're wearing a stolen shape that obscures your Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:22:50-07:00","id":928103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=927853#post927853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, but I have no acceptable rebuttal prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the magical thing about these kinds of threads - you are under no obligation to rush out a rebuttal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:41:00-07:00","id":930035,"title":"","content":"<i>Lunar HEAVEN THUNDER HAMMER</i><br /> <b>FOE-DRIVING ATTACK</b><br /> <br /> <i>3m; Reflexive, Instant; Decisive-only; Strength 3, Essence 1 \u2013 ???</i><br /> <br /> This Charm is activated after a successful decisive attack, before rolling for damage.<br /> <br /> If the damage roll generates at least one success, the target is knocked prone by the force of the blow, and loses a point of Initiative, which is added to the Lunar's base value when her Initiative resets.<br /> <br /> For at least three successes, the opponent is lifted and bodily hurled into an object or surface within close range, hitting it with an impact equivalent to falling a short distance, destroying any less-obdurate objects they collide with, such as wooden furniture.<br /> <br /> At four or more successes, the foe is knocked into an object at close range with tremendous force, or is sent sailing a remarkable distance by the force of the blow. If the former, the opponent hits a surface with force sufficient to leave cracks in a stone wall, impacting with a surface as if they had fallen from a medium distance. If the latter, the force of the blow throws them to short range with a short-distance falling impact.<br /> <br /> At five or more successes, the foe is thrown to short range and suffers an impact like falling from a medium height.<br /> <br /> When the Lunar uses this Charm to supplement a Decisive smashing attack and achieves at least one success, she is treated as having scored three additional successes solely for the purpose of determining the distance the victim is hurled. However, the Lunar does not gain the victim's lost point of Initiative.<br /> <br /> If this smashing attack naturally receives benefits equivalent to the Solar Charm, Heaven Thunder Hammer, the Lunar instead doubles her successes for the purposes of this Charm and, at Essence 5+, may use seven or more successes to hurl the victim out to medium range with a medium height impact.<br /> <br /> As per the Solar Charm, Heaven Thunder Hammer, players are encouraged to use the environment to enhance this Charm's effectiveness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>IRRESISTIBLE STORM ATTACK</b><br /> <br /> <i>+2m; Permanent; No keywords; Strength 5, Essence 3 -- Foe-Driving Attack</i><br /> <br /> By paying two additional motes, the Lunar may use this Charm's prerequisite with a projectile attack.<br /> <br /> Smaller projectiles such as throwing knives and arrows reduce the Lunar's successes by three for the purposes of Foe-Driving Attack. A projectile as large as a man imposes no penalty. A projectile larger than a man but smaller than a creature with Legendary Size increases the effective successes by three if any successes are scored at all. A projectile as large as a creature with Legendary Size instead doubles the effective successes. A projectile larger than even <i>that</i> may allow the victim to be hurled out to medium range with a medium height impact if the Lunar scores seven or more successes.<br /> <br /> This Charm by itself confers the Lunar no ability to throw greater weights than usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-11-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:23:46-07:00","id":930045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=930035#post930035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this smashing attack naturally receives benefits equivalent to the Solar Charm, Heaven Thunder Hammer, the Lunar instead doubles her successes for the purposes of this Charm and, at Essence 5+, may use seven or more successes to hurl the victim out to medium range with a medium height impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little hesitant about this. I feel like splat charms should be distinct in reference: If it has the same benefits, it has the same benefits. I don't think there's anything inherently wrong with that, and having it reference another charm is more booking for both the player and the ST, especially if they don't have that splat open. The language is also a little vague for me: What does it mean for something to &quot;naturally receive the benefits equivalent to Heaven Thunder Hammer&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:27:29-07:00","id":930079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=930045#post930045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little hesitant about this. I feel like splat charms should be distinct in reference: If it has the same benefits, it has the same benefits. I don't think there's anything inherently wrong with that, and having it reference another charm is more booking for both the player and the ST, especially if they don't have that splat open.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only part of the Charm that heavily references Heaven Thunder Hammer is alluding to the mechanically <i>softest</i> part of that Solar Charm.<br /> <br /> If you're using the Lunar book, then you're already working off the Solar-filled corebook. Heaven Thunder Hammer is one of the more popular and memorable Charms, especially the part where you can use it to punt people off of cliffs, or into ceilings so that they can hit the ceiling and then hit the floor for twice as many sources of pain. This Lunar Charm is saying, &quot;you can be as creative with this as with that Solar Charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> The crunchier mechanics are fully detailed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The language is also a little vague for me: What does it mean for something to &quot;naturally receive the benefits equivalent to Heaven Thunder Hammer&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The special tail attacks of the Pestletail and Siege Lizard explicitly say that they mimic the effects of Heaven Thunder Hammer. Those and regular old maces are what I'm balancing this Charm around.<br /> <br /> And if you wanted to be a Lunar in one of those forms, you'd have to be referencing the corebook for those beasts anyway, and those beasts already reference that particular Solar Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:50:58-07:00","id":930096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=930079#post930079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only part of the Charm that heavily references Heaven Thunder Hammer is alluding to the mechanically <i>softest</i> part of that Solar Charm.<br /> <br /> If you're using the Lunar book, then you're already working off the Solar-filled corebook. Heaven Thunder Hammer is one of the more popular and memorable Charms, especially the part where you can use it to punt people off of cliffs, or into ceilings so that they can hit the ceiling and then hit the floor for twice as many sources of pain. This Lunar Charm is saying, &quot;you can be as creative with this as with that Solar Charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> The crunchier mechanics are fully detailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but as a reader, I didn't ynderstand that the creative portion is what you're talking about. I didn't see a reference to it in any real way, I only saw additional mechanical differences. I think some clarity about what you meant would have helped because the charm already strongly resembles the solar charm, so I didn't understand what I was supposed to take away from the referent, except that it doubles successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/922985-ex3-lunar-size-strength-limits-and-charms?p=930079#post930079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The special tail attacks of the Pestletail and Siege Lizard explicitly say that they mimic the effects of Heaven Thunder Hammer. Those and regular old maces are what I'm balancing this Charm around.<br /> <br /> And if you wanted to be a Lunar in one of those forms, you'd have to be referencing the corebook for those beasts anyway, and those beasts already reference that particular Solar Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more quibbling about the term &quot;naturally receives benefits equivalent to&quot;. The Siege Lizard and the Pestletail both say that they grant the benefits of the charm, not anything about an &quot;if&quot; condition and the word &quot;naturally.&quot;I didn't - and I still don't - really understand what the &quot;if&quot; is doing in that sentence. Hence my question, what does it mean for something to naturally receive a benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":". 07-12-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}